  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Scope**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the scope for a new web application. My thoughts center on tracking truck trip information, and I\'ve started by examining the existing manual system, which is a table with columns like truck number, origin, destination, driver, date, distance, and fuel used. This provides a baseline.\n\n\n**Structuring the Data**\n\nI\'m now structuring the data sheets. I\'ve got a master truck list with registration, owner, model, and status. There\'s also an office sheet with name, location, and contact. Furthermore, I am planning an account sheet for financial entries, considering cash, bank, employee, and GPay options. I\'m focusing on autogenerated trip numbers and the relationship between multiple entries composing a single trip.\n\n\n**Integrating Account References**\n\nI\'m integrating account references, specifically for advance and balance payments, using dropdown selections from the accounts list. This is key for showing where funds are received. I\'m also refining the trip and entry tracking. I\'m focusing on \"Trip No\" generation, allowing for autogeneration, selection, or new trip creation, and its relationship to individual entries, using dropdowns for Truck No and Office Name, for instance.\n\n\n**Refining Payment Fields**\n\nI\'m refining the payment fields for each entry now, adding specific fields for Rental, Loading Date, Commission, and Loading/Unloading charges. I\'m including Office Mamul for local expenses, and three advance payment fields with corresponding dates and \"Received By\" dropdowns linked to the Accounts master. Thinking further about the \"Balance\" field, I\'m considering if it\'s auto-calculated (Rental - Commission - Loading/Unloading - Office Mamul - Advances) instead of manually entered, reflecting the revenue less deductions.\n\n\n**Calculating the Balance**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the \"Balance\" field and its calculation. Initially, I thought about simply calculating it, but I\'ve decided to make it flexible. The field will show the formula and allow manual override, or a calculated formula: `Balance = Rental - Commission - LoadingUnloading - OfficeMamul - Advance1 - Advance2 - Advance3`. I\'m also adding \"Balance\" date and \"Received By\" dropdowns, linked to the Accounts master, plus a Status dropdown: \"Pending\", \"In Progress\", \"Completed\", \"Paid\". I am also considering a local storage/localStorage integration.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Local Persistence**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing local persistence using `localStorage`. This approach offers simplicity, responsiveness, and avoids unnecessary external dependencies unless explicitly requested. I will implement an \"Export to Backup / Import from Backup\" feature for JSON data backups. I\'m focusing on building a high-quality SPA with great tables, filters, and financial summaries. Finally, I\'ll update `metadata.json`.\n\n\n**Defining the Architecture**\n\nI\'m now defining the application\'s basic architecture. I\'ve chosen the title \"Truck Trip Tracker\" and the description \"Track and manage truck trips, rental payments, commissions, advances, and outstanding balances with master data sheets.\" I\'ll use TypeScript and focus on creating modular components within a `/src/components/` directory. These components include `TruckMaster`, `OfficeMaster`, `AccountMaster`, `TripForm`, `Dashboard`, and `TripList`.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will start by viewing the `metadata.json` file to inspect its content and update the application name and description to be descriptive and professional."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 677576407
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
