    thinking: "**Constructing Datasheets**\n\nI\'m now focused on building the master datasheets. My current plan is to develop an elegant interface with tabs. I\'ll include a dashboard tab for financial summaries, totals, and visual status highlights. The trips and entries tab will handle the main workflow table and associated functions.\n\n\n**Defining Default Datasheets**\n\nI\'m now populating the master datasheets with default entries to enhance initial usability and aesthetics. I\'m focusing on preloading the app with sample data, including truck, office, and account details. This will showcase a functional application right from the start, demonstrating real-world transaction examples. The user will be able to either generate a new trip number or choose an existing trip number when entering data.\n\n\n**Designing Input Flow**\n\nI\'ve crafted a really helpful input flow for the TripForm. It has a slick \"Trip Number\" field with two options: \"Start New Trip No,\" auto-suggesting an incremented trip number, and \"Associate with Existing Trip,\" presenting a dropdown of recent trip numbers. This simplifies creating a new trip or adding to an existing one. A custom sequence generator will suggest the next trip number, and components are being designed for absolute modularity.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now create `/src/components/TruckMaster.tsx` to handle the Truck Datasheet. It will allow adding, editing, and deleting trucks from the master list, showing their status, owner details, and driver information. This master data acts as the select source for the Trip Entry form."
