ckup, Restore). I\'m looking at fitting these actions into the header bar or as a secondary buttons group inside the header or the top of the content area. I\'m focusing on a design for the main content area\'s header to include the title & total counts badge.\n\n\n**Refining Button Designs**\n\nI\'m now refining the button styles to match the desired \"Professional Polish\" look. I\'m focusing on the light gray button styling, ensuring it has the correct border, hover effect, and text color. I\'m also confirming the primary \"Post Entry\" button. Now, I\'m examining `/src/App.tsx` and focusing on the structural transition from lines 400 to 646.\n\n\n**Implementing Sidebar Layout**\n\nI\'m now implementing the sidebar layout, mirroring the HTML structure. I\'m focusing on the outer container in `App.tsx` and ensuring the layout matches the desired sidebar design. I\'m making sure all the components fit the layout. My focus now is in perfecting the structural transition.\n\n\n**Styling Active States**\n\nI\'m now implementing the sidebar active states using Tailwind classes like `bg-blue-600/10` and `text-blue-400`. I\'m using `onClick` events in my Javascript logic to adjust styles, ensuring that the selected tab, such as \'Dashboard\', has its design updated when it is active. I\'m focusing on making the selection visually clear and responsive.\n\n\n**Refining Tab Styles**\n\nI\'m now refining the tab styles for \"Trip Management\", \"Truck Registry\" and \"Offices\" using the provided Tailwind classes. I\'m focusing on ensuring the active state uses `bg-blue-600/10` and `text-blue-400` while the default state is `text-slate-400` and `hover:text-white`. I\'m using `onClick` events to manage the active tab state and applying `font-semibold` when the tab is active.\n\n\n**Implementing Tab Navigation**\n\nI\'m now implementing the tab navigation for \"Account Ledger\", making sure the active state and hover effects are consistent with the other tabs. I\'m leveraging Tailwind classes to manage the active state (`bg-blue-600/10`, `text-blue-400`, `font-semibold`) and the default/hover states (`text-slate-400`, `hover:text-white`). I\'m using `onClick` events to update the state.\n\n\n**Designing System Status**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating the system status indicator in the sidebar, specifically the \"Local Sync Online\" status. I\'m styling the indicator using Tailwind classes, including a green pulse animation for a visual cue. I\'m aiming for a subtle yet informative presentation, using a small, rounded green indicator and concise text.\n\n\n**Structuring Header Elements**\n\nI\'m now structuring the header elements, incorporating the title, total counts badge, and utility actions. I\'m focusing on responsiveness, ensuring the layout adapts gracefully across different screen sizes. I am particularly considering the placement of the \"Seeding\" button, deciding between the header bar or a secondary group.\n\n\n**Defining Utility Actions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing and integrating utility actions like \"Seed Data,\" \"Backup,\" and \"Restore\" buttons into the header. I\'m choosing a clean, professional look with light backgrounds and subtle hover effects, utilizing Tailwind classes for border and shadow styles. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and clarity, ensuring each button clearly conveys its function. I\'m also including concise text labels and icons for better user understanding.\n\n\n\n**Integrating Restore Feature**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Restore\" button functionality within the header. I\'ve added an `input` element to upload `.json` files, linking the button click with this file input and attaching an `onChange` event to update the state. I\'m focusing on ensuring data recovery is user-friendly and doesn\'t interrupt workflow.\n\n\n"
