    modified_response: "I have completed the refactoring of the ledger payments system and completed outstanding tasks to support an unlimited, dynamic register of payments.\n\n### \360\237\214\237 Summary of Highlights & Design Concepts\n\n* **Unlimited Receipts Ledger (`N` Payments)**:\n  - Replaced the hardcoded three-stage advances with a nested, highly flexible payments grid directly inside **Transport Trip Segment**.\n  - Users can input **Payment Date**, select from **Active Account Ledgers**, set an **Amount (\342\202\271)**, and attach **Purpose / Remarks** (e.g., fuel advance, driver compensation, toll expense).\n  - Any logged payment instantly updates the dynamic calculations and decreases the liabilities.\n\n* **Interactive Trip Journal**:\n  - The **Trip Journal Table** now totals and aggregates all dynamic payment receipts dynamically for each line.\n  - Refined the visual slide-over **Document Log Auditor** (Inspect View) to render structured cards for each stored payment in the trip log history.\n\n* **Smart Auto-Reporting CSV Exports**:\n  - Rewrote the spreadsheet exporter to compile structured financial listings, gross contract values, cumulative received amounts, and exact remaining balances.\n  - Generates self-documenting inline **Payments Logs Details** (e.g., `\"\342\202\27115,000 on 10/05 (Bank Account - Stage 1) | \342\202\2715,500 on 12/05 (Petty Cash - Fuel)\"`) allowing accountants to analyze receipts in one clean column without structural clutter.\n\n* **Refined Real-Time Formula Engine**:\n  - Calculations update reactively as payments are added or deleted in real-time, instantly shifting status tags between **Pending**, **In Progress**, and **Paid** based on outstanding obligations.\n"
