    thinking: "**Analyzing Trip Structure**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s desire to revamp the trip management structure. My focus is on understanding the core components of the new \"Trip\" entity: the `Truck No`, `Trip No`, `Trip Start Date`, `Trip End Date`, `Driver Name`, and derived `Income`. I\'m starting to visualize how these attributes interact and their implications for the overall system.\n\n\n**Defining Trip Data Points**\n\nNow, I\'m defining specific data columns and expense types. The core columns, like `Truck No`, `Trip No`, and dates are established. Expenses are detailed, including `Loading`, `Unloading`, `RTO`, `Diesel` (with liters, rate, and amount), `Add Blue`, `Fastag`, and `Driver Wages`. I\'m also including `Starting KM`, `Ending KM`, and calculations for `Total KM`, `Millage`, `Per KM`, and `No of Days`. I\'m planning a `Total Expense` summation.\n\n\n**Structuring Trip Relationships**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the hierarchical relationship between \"Trips\" and \"Sub Trips\". My aim is to establish a clear structure where a single \"Trip\" can encompass multiple \"Sub Trips,\" each with its own specific details, expenses, and location data. I am thinking about how to connect the \"Sub Trip\" data such as from/to, income, expense, and loading/unloading into the main \"Trip\".\n\n\n**Aggregating Trip Data**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into aggregating data for Master Trips from their Sub Trips. The goal is to automatically calculate key metrics: Income, all expense types (loading, unloading, etc.), fuel liters, starting and ending KM (with an option for manual edits). My focus is on creating a system where the Master Trip provides a clear, summarized view derived from its Sub Trip components. I\'m prioritizing the efficient and automatic aggregation of expenses.\n\n\n**Calculating Trip Metrics**\n\nI\'ve finalized formulas for `KM`, `Millage`, `Per KM`, `No of Days`, `Total Expense`, and `Profit`, ensuring edge case handling. I\'m now structuring the Master Trip and Sub Trip data layout, focusing on a clear user experience. I\'m prioritizing the user\'s workflow - can they create a Master Trip and then enter Sub Trips, or can they add/edit them directly inside the Master Trip view? Also, I\'ve incorporated the account payments feature with amount, account, and date.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view `/src/types.ts` to understand the current structure and prepare the types for our master trip revamp."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 866651053
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
