t` function. My focus is on writing robust helper functions in `src/types` to ensure consistency and shareability of these computed values across components.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Migration**\n\nI\'m now writing migration code within the app to handle older, pre-update trip data, ensuring a seamless transition and preventing errors for existing users. I will implement a `migrateTripsIfNecessary` function that automatically adapts to the new trip data format. I\'m also re-examining `src/types.ts` and the associated fields, including the `TripPayment` and `SubTrip` structures to make sure data is properly handled.\n\n\n**Defining Trip Interface**\n\nI am now solidifying the data structures for trips and their related metrics. I\'ve defined `TripMetrics` and the complete `SubTrip` data structure. I am working on the overall trip definition and refining the interfaces and helpers needed for easy computation of trip data, including fields like loading, unloading, RTO, diesel (liters, rate, and total), addBlue, fastag, driver wages, and other expenses.\n\n\n**Calculating Financial Metrics**\n\nI\'m now calculating various financial metrics, focusing on their implementation. I am calculating `paymentsReceived`, `outstandingBalance`, and other summary trip metrics such as `income`, `loadingExpense`, and other expense types based on their `subTrips` values, and I am incorporating a robust reduction function. I am now incorporating all of these values into a single helper function, `getTripMetrics`.\n\n\n**Refining Expense Calculations**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on accurate expense calculations. I\'m focusing on the helper functions to calculate expenses and trip data accurately. I\'ve integrated `driverWages`, `otherExpense`, `fuelLiters`, `totalKM` calculations, and the `millage` metric. Also included are `totalExpense`, `profit`, and `perKM`. I\'m verifying and testing the helper functions that compute these values to ensure data integrity.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will edit `/src/types.ts` to declare the new models: `SubTrip`, `TripEntry`, `TripMetrics`, and the computed metric getter `getTripMetrics()`. This keeps our business logic modular and self-documenting."
