is a solid start.\n\n\n**Visualizing Trip List Design**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the user interface for `TripList.tsx`. My current focus is on a clear and visually appealing display of trip data using a grid or table format. The default view will include key details like Trip ID, Truck Number, Driver Name, dates, income, expenses, profit, and status. I plan to enhance the user experience by using JetBrains Mono for numbers and customized labels for clarity. Furthermore, the design will support expansion or selection of rows to access detailed sub-trip information.\n\n\n**Implementing Detailed Display**\n\nI\'ve sketched out the next phase of `TripList.tsx`\'s design. The plan is to enhance the row expansion feature. Clicking a row will show two new elements: a sub-trip list as a child table (with light borders and specific metrics), and a master trip summary box (using a Bento Grid with Odometer, Duration, and Profitability stats). I\'m planning this for a desktop-first responsive design using Tailwind, and will write the new `TripList.tsx` from scratch, replacing the legacy code. I want to build this as a professional desktop-first responsive layout with standard Tailwind.\n\n\n"
