ce, perhaps by refining the visual hierarchy of these elements.\n\n\n**Refining Dropdown Styles**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the styling of the ledger account and sub-trip dropdowns. I\'m assessing the effectiveness of the `text-xs` and `font-semibold` classes, and the overall border and background styling. I\'m considering adjustments to improve visual clarity and ensure a consistent look across different options within each dropdown. My goal is to enhance user legibility.\n\n\n**Assessing Numeric Input**\n\nI\'m now examining the settled amount input field\'s styling, specifically its Tailwind classes. I\'m focusing on the number input with `text-right` and `font-mono`, while also considering the payment notes input. I\'m thinking about the user\'s perception of these elements and ways to improve how they perceive and use the fields. I\'m striving for increased clarity, aesthetics, and user interaction.\n\n\n**Improving Button Interactions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the interaction and styling of the \"+ Register\" button, specifically how the Tailwind classes, such as `bg-blue-600` and `hover:bg-blue-700`, impact its behavior and appearance. I\'m also considering the integration of the segment name display within the payments list table, and how this could improve user understanding and ease of use. I\'m taking into account the font styles. I\'m aiming to make the registration process more intuitive.\n\n\n**Clarifying Segment Display**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the table header\'s \"Purpose / Segment Memo\". I\'m thinking of replacing this column header with one that specifies the related segment from the subtrip object\'s data, which enhances clarity for each payment row. I am updating the table\'s contents to clarify each row\'s segment.\n\n\n"
