r CRUD**\n\nI\'m now integrating the CRUD operations for driver management. I\'ve implemented `handleAddDriver`, which includes checks to prevent duplicate names and utilizes `saveDrivers` to ensure state updates. I have also added `handleUpdateDriver` for editing drivers. Finally, I\'ve incorporated `handleDeleteDriver` with trip assignment checks to ensure that a driver is not deleted if they are currently assigned to an active road journey, which also utilizes `saveDrivers`. All three include notifications.\n\n\n**Adding Seed Data Reset**\n\nI\'m now integrating a data reset feature. I\'ve added code around lines 283 and 300 to restore seed data for trucks, drivers, offices, accounts, and trips. I\'m verifying data loading from a JSON file, along with restoring defaults via `confirm()`. I\'m working on restoring the local storage using the `saveTrucks` functions. I\'m also adding a button to call the function in the UI.\n\n\n**Refining Tab Implementation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the tab implementation within the UI. I\'m carefully examining the conditional rendering logic for different tabs, specifically the \'TRUCKS\', \'OFFICES\', \'DRIVERS\', and \'ACCOUNTS\' tabs. I am examining how to implement the tab\'s visual attributes and event handlers, as well.\n\nI am paying close attention to ensuring that the active tab state properly updates the visual indicators, such as background color and text formatting, which correctly reflects the user\'s selection.\n\n\n**Finalizing Tab Display**\n\nI\'m now integrating tab-specific content and summaries into the UI. I\'ve worked on dynamic content for different tabs; for the Drivers tab I\'m updating the component, and also checking for the correct display of trucks, offices, accounts, and drivers summaries, as well. I\'m focusing on lines 700 to ensure component rendering aligns with the active tab state, including data display.\n\n\n"
