  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have successfully completed the refactoring and integration work for the **FleetTrack Pro** trip management system. The application has passed typescript validation and successfully built into standard static files.\n\n### \360\237\222\274 Technical and Operational Highlights\n\n- **Master Driver Registry & Integration**: \n  - Created a robust, dedicated **Driver Database** view aligned with the other master sheets (Trucks, Offices, Accounts).\n  - Wired custom CRUD operations loaded from and persisted to local storage, complete with built-in reference checking to prevent the deletion of drivers tied to historical trips.\n  - Linked the modal trip planner driver inputs to dynamically populate from this master driver database.\n  \n- **Cargo Segment Optimization**:\n  - Refactored the core cargo subtrip panels to house only segment-specific costs (**Income**, **Cargo Loading Expenses**, **Cargo Unloading Expenses**, and **Driver Wages**).\n  - Consolidated common overland trip expenditures (**RTO permits**, **AdBlue cost**, **Fastag toll charges**, **diesel fuel rate calculations**, and **miscellaneous expenses**) as a single unified master journey block.\n\n- **Leg-Specific Financial Settlement Receipts**:\n  - Upgraded the receipt/advances tracker to support tagging payments either as **Leg-Specific Segment payments** (tracking office-by-office pending balances) or **General Trip payments**.\n  - Restructured the financial ledger list to clearly visualize segment references and linked offices, allowing operators to monitor exactly which office is pending settlement.\n\n- **Comprehensive Seeding, Backup & Recovery**:\n  - Extended the JSON backup, reader uploads, and data seeding engine to wrap the new driver definitions securely, facilitating fully offline data retention."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
