  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Fuel Input Options**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user\'s request for multiple fuel input options. The challenge is clear: moving beyond a single \"diesel\" entry to accommodate diverse fuel types, each with associated parameters like liters, rate, and date. I am considering the structure to allow a flexible number of fuel entries. I will need to consider date entry.\n\n\n**Structuring Fuel Listings**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the ability to add multiple fuel entries. I\'m exploring a sub-array structure within the trip details to efficiently manage these listings. I\'ve noted the requirement for the ability to add, remove, and sum fuel entries, as well as the need for date entry and station notes. I am checking existing structures for relevant types.\n\n**Adding Driver Wages Logic**\n\nOkay, I\'m now tasked with incorporating a driver wages/allowance calculation based on a percentage of the segment income. The plan is to include a helper UI element within `TripForm.tsx` that allows a percentage selection (1-20%). The chosen percentage will then be multiplied by the segment\'s income to determine the wages/allowance, which will be automatically registered.\n\n\n**Implementing Dashboard Displays**\n\nI am now structuring the dashboard to show outstanding balances categorized by truck. The plan is to present unpaid/pending/remaining balances associated with each truck. I\'m exploring interactive elements \342\200\223 tooltips or styled popovers \342\200\223 to display detailed breakdowns upon hover. This will include office, loading details (route, contract income), advance payments, and the remaining balance.\n\n**Adding Truck Datasheet Details**\n\nI am now focusing on restructuring the truck datasheet. I\'ve noted the need to remove driver details and replace them with a new set of fields. The objective is to include details like Make, Model, Type, Insurance information, FC data, Pinpush KM, Wheel Grease KM, Alignment dates, Q Tax, and Green Tax information.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will open the `src/types.ts` file to see how we define the state schemas and find the best way to extend them with the new requirements."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 664570743
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
