\n**Defining Maintenance Metrics**\n\nI\'m now integrating maintenance-related properties into the `Truck` interface within `types.ts`. I\'m determining how to calculate and display the remaining days for various permits, like the five-year permit, and I\'m updating properties such as `currentKM` and adding target mileage for oil changes. I\'m focusing on \"Engine Oil KM Left,\" which will be calculated as `engineOilKM - currentKM`, and the same logic applies to crown, gearbox, and radiator oil maintenance. Finally, I\'ll incorporate a truck `status` property.\n\n\n**Refactoring Truck Data**\n\nI\'m now focusing on removing the `driverName` and `phone` fields from the `Truck` interface and updating `src/types.ts`. I have to verify that removing these fields does not break any parts of `TripForm.tsx` that might be relying on them. The current solution involves keeping `driverName` as optional in `Truck` in `types.ts`, however, the user requested that \"under truck datasheet remove driver details and add below details\". I will remove the fields from the visual form and datasheet views.\n\n\n**Implementing Truck Data Fields**\n\nI\'ve decided to maintain `driverName` in the `Truck` schema as optional for data integrity and backward compatibility, while removing it from the UI datasheet and replacing it with detailed vehicle parameters. The plan is to list the essential properties for the `Truck` interface, including `make`, `model`, `type`, various expiry dates for permits and taxes, `currentKM`, and target mileage for maintenance.\n\n\n"
